Challenge 116 — Identify the Git Service Port

Question:
Identify the port on which Git service is running on the machine 192.168.1.151.

Answer Format: NNNN

Step 1: Scan the target

Use Nmap service detection:

nmap -sV 192.168.1.151

This scans the common ports and attempts to identify the services running on them.

Step 2: Analyze the output

The scan showed:

PORT     STATE SERVICE VERSION
22/tcp   open  ssh     OpenSSH 7.6p1 Ubuntu 4ubuntu0.3
80/tcp   open  http    Apache httpd 2.4.29
3000/tcp open  http    Golang net/http server

The Git service was not directly identified by Nmap, so we inspect the response from port 3000.

Step 3: Identify the Git service

The Nmap service fingerprint contains:

Set-Cookie: i_like_gitea=...

The keyword gitea is the important clue.

Gitea is a Git hosting service. Therefore, the HTTP service running on port 3000 is Gitea.

We can also scan all TCP ports to make sure there isn't another Git service:

nmap -p- -sV 192.168.1.151

The result again shows:

3000/tcp open http
Step 4: Determine the answer

Since Gitea/Git service is running on port 3000, the answer is:

3000
Final Answer

Challenge 116 → 3000
